@Green-Sky [Edited] I'm still trying to figure this out myself, so I may be wrong about the chronology. I can only see that there was a merge with Zoxcore, followed by commit 849281ea — Add a way to fetch groups by chat ID https://github.com/TokTok/c-toxcore/commit/849281ea.

In the current tox.h I found this:

Tox_Group_Number tox_group_join(
	Tox *tox, const Tox_Group_Chat_Id chat_id,
	const uint8_t name[], size_t name_length,
	const uint8_t password[], size_t password_length,
	Tox_Err_Group_Join *error);

However, it seems that in the version I have on disk, the tox_group_join function inside tox.h is completely missing.

In Zoxcore, it has different parameters:

uint32_t tox_group_join(
	Tox *tox,
	const uint8_t *chat_id,
	const uint8_t *name,
	size_t name_length,
	const uint8_t *password,
	size_t password_length,
	Tox_Err_Group_Join *error);

In your version of toxcore:

Tox_Group_Number tox_group_join(
	Tox *tox,
	const Tox_Group_Chat_Id chat_id,
	const uint8_t name[],
	size_t name_length,
	const uint8_t password[], size_t password_length,
	Tox_Err_Group_Join *error);

I think I need to download the current version from your repository. Right now I'm trying to compile my test C++ group-chat code against the older Zoxcore version. If I figure it out, I'll make a branch. If not, maybe someone else will figure it out someday. :)
